  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far (config_013, acc=0.542) uses multiprofile + scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted fusion. Moving from singleprofile→multiprofile gave +8.3% acc, and concat→weighted fusion gave +2.4% acc, confirming that richer profile aggregation and learned fusion weights help. The key remaining uncertainty is whether a more expressive aggregation mechanism (transformer attention) can outperform simple average pooling when combining multiple profiles. This experiment (config_035) tests exactly that: it swaps avgpool→transformer while keeping all other settings identical to the current best (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, weighted, multiprofile). If transformer aggregation captures inter-profile relationships better than mean pooling, we expect a meaningful accuracy gain; if not, it confirms avgpool is sufficient and we can pivot to other axes (e.g., RNA encoder or image encoder). Cost: transformer aggregation adds self-attention layers over profiles, so I estimate ~4–6 GPU hours (moderately more expensive than config_013's 2.94 h but well within budget). This is the highest-value exploitation step: it directly extends the best-known direction with a single, well-motivated change, and with 6 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out transformer aggregation early will guide the rest of the search efficiently."
}

